NeRFax source bundled with ciMIST
===============================

This directory contains a locally modified copy of NeRFax:
https://github.com/PeptoneLtd/nerfax

The upstream source is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The license text is retained in ciMIST's root LICENSE and included with its
source and wheel distributions. This notice describes ciMIST modifications;
it does not change the license terms or imply upstream endorsement.

The changes below are described relative to upstream reference
8d04e1a919c7a86ad9372917b12de3991a117cbe, also cited by ciMIST's trajectory
converter. The original vendoring revision was not recorded. That reference
contains no upstream NOTICE file.

Files modified for ciMIST:

- parser.py: topology-aware residue and atom mapping; supported-residue,
  atom and bond validation; selection with intact covalent context; physical
  feature masks; periodic imaging and batched geometry; trajectory loader
  and scaffold adaptations.
- plugin.py: package-relative reconstruction import; initialization of
  reconstruction-only ghost references; rejection of unsupported
  reconstruction geometries.
- reconstruct.py: package-relative callback import; public jax.Device import
  and jax.tree_util.tree_map compatibility updates.
- utils.py: package-relative reconstruction import.

In addition, ../trajectory.py adapts the converter from upstream plugin.py:
it retains ciMIST's bond-angle convention instead of applying the upstream
pi-minus-angle conversion, and integrates it with trajectory extraction
and reconstruction.

Existing source credits to EleutherAI/mp_nerf and Google JAX are retained.
